WEBVTT

00:02.210 --> 00:04.330
<i>What a relaxing dream!</i>

00:05.600 --> 00:08.270
Ryuto, it's morning time.

00:08.840 --> 00:10.900
<i>I hear Shirakawa-san's voice...</i>

00:19.400 --> 00:21.660
Ryuto! How long are you gonna stay in bed?

00:21.660 --> 00:23.060
Ahh!

00:23.620 --> 00:25.240
Good morning.

00:25.240 --> 00:27.050
G-Good morning.

00:28.520 --> 00:31.050
<i>It isn't a dream!</i>

00:31.680 --> 00:38.120
<i>During the summer, I get to live 
under the same roof as Shirakawa-san!</i>

00:50.480 --> 00:57.110
<b>Our Dating Story: 
The Experienced You and The Inexperienced Me</b>

02:08.980 --> 02:13.770
<b>Our Festival Story: The Experienced You</b>

02:09.500 --> 02:13.770
<b>and the Inexperienced Me</b>

02:10.000 --> 02:13.770
<b>Go to a Summer Festival.</b>

02:12.280 --> 02:13.770
Welcome!

02:13.770 --> 02:15.820
Shaved ice with strawberry, please.

02:15.820 --> 02:17.240
I'll have melon.

02:17.240 --> 02:18.820
All right!

02:18.820 --> 02:21.120
I'd like to rent a locker.

02:21.120 --> 02:22.530
A-All right!

02:22.530 --> 02:25.660
With a hot shower, it's um...

02:26.070 --> 02:27.870
1,000 yen per person.

02:27.870 --> 02:29.790
Sounds good to me.

02:29.790 --> 02:31.470
Thank you very much!

02:31.470 --> 02:33.420
Um, th-thunks.

02:32.080 --> 02:35.710
<b>Ice</b>

02:40.010 --> 02:41.840
<b>Ryuto</b>

02:41.840 --> 02:43.600
<b>From Mom</b>

02:45.410 --> 02:47.890
<b>Runa</b>

02:50.180 --> 02:53.350
Ryuto, why don't you take your break now?

02:53.350 --> 02:54.140
Sure.

03:00.950 --> 03:02.620
Hey, Runa-chan!

03:02.620 --> 03:04.330
You're back today.

03:04.650 --> 03:07.040
Hello and... welcome.

03:08.500 --> 03:09.880
You all alone?

03:09.880 --> 03:12.080
You sure are cute, Runa-chan.

03:12.960 --> 03:16.800
<i>Clearly the popular type.
 And obvious players!</i>

03:17.160 --> 03:19.320
So where you stayin'? Nearby?

03:20.510 --> 03:22.620
Oh, come on, don't be that way.

03:22.620 --> 03:24.720
<i>What are those guys doing?</i>

03:25.040 --> 03:28.590
<i>And right when Mao-san
 is out getting supplies!</i>

03:28.590 --> 03:30.120
...right, Runa-chan?

03:28.930 --> 03:30.650
<i>They're so scary!</i>

03:30.650 --> 03:33.920
So like, between me and him, 
who would you pick?

03:33.920 --> 03:34.750
Uh...

03:34.750 --> 03:36.480
Totally me. Right, Runa-chan?

03:36.480 --> 03:39.210
But this guy's a total chicken.

03:39.210 --> 03:40.830
Who the hell are you calling a chicken?

03:40.830 --> 03:42.510
U-Um...

03:43.240 --> 03:47.410
A-Are you here for a locker? Or a meal?

03:47.410 --> 03:48.860
Uh...

03:50.230 --> 03:53.580
Part-timer? So you weren't a customer?

03:54.020 --> 03:56.050
Yo, wanna bounce?

03:56.050 --> 03:58.330
Runa-chan, we'll come again.

04:01.840 --> 04:06.260
So hey, between the part-timer, me, 
and this guy, who'd you pick?

04:08.650 --> 04:11.980
I pick him. Since he's my boyfriend.

04:12.660 --> 04:14.260
<i>Shirakawa-san...</i>

04:16.710 --> 04:18.300
Didn't see that coming.

04:18.300 --> 04:19.580
I'm so done.

04:19.580 --> 04:20.530
Screw this.

04:21.530 --> 04:26.410
I hate it so much! It's always
 guys like that who try to talk to me.

04:26.410 --> 04:30.040
I'm sorry I didn't help you sooner.

04:30.040 --> 04:34.510
Actually, thanks! I'm so glad you were here.

04:38.340 --> 04:43.300
You sure do work hard, Ryuto. 
You study every day, even at the beach.

04:43.300 --> 04:48.760
Well, when my parents sent my clothes, 
they packed in all my school stuff, too.

04:48.760 --> 04:52.540
You're so smart, I bet you'll get 
into a great college, Ryuto.

04:52.540 --> 04:54.920
N-No way! I'm not even close.

04:54.920 --> 04:57.260
I'm still impressed, though.

04:57.260 --> 05:03.160
Nicole is planning to go to a manicurist
school after graduation to get certified.

05:03.160 --> 05:04.320
Huh.

05:04.320 --> 05:09.180
But Nicole's mom is a single mother, 
so she can't count on money from her parents.

05:09.180 --> 05:13.750
That's why she's working all the time. 
To save up money for tuition.

05:13.750 --> 05:15.940
I didn't know that.

05:15.940 --> 05:20.340
Akari, too. She says she 
wants to go to fashion school.

05:20.820 --> 05:24.420
Everyone else already has 
their future figured out.

05:24.420 --> 05:28.140
What about you? 
What are you doing after graduation?

05:29.730 --> 05:33.350
You know, I'm kinda feeling
 a little burnt out.

05:34.050 --> 05:38.500
I've already achieved the goal I set 
for my high school years anyway.

05:38.500 --> 05:39.640
Goal?

05:40.900 --> 05:45.280
To develop mutual feelings with 
someone I think I can stay with forever.

05:46.440 --> 05:50.140
I was actually looking 
for a place to settle down.

05:52.710 --> 05:59.380
Living with Dad and Mom and Maria again 
like before was always my biggest dream.

06:00.710 --> 06:05.590
But if that didn't work, 
then I wanted to build my own family.

06:06.130 --> 06:11.930
I'd be a mom, have lots of kids, 
and have a husband I'm truly in love with.

06:11.930 --> 06:14.930
We'd always act lovey-dovey, 
even with the kids around.

06:14.930 --> 06:18.140
Oh, is that too much?
 I bet it sounds like too much.

06:18.140 --> 06:19.900
No, it isn't too much.

06:20.820 --> 06:25.670
<i>Shirakawa-san has spent a lot more time 
thinking about the future than I have.</i>

06:27.190 --> 06:30.280
<i>Even about her future with me.</i>

06:38.580 --> 06:42.520
<i>I'd better study harder for my college exams.</i>

06:42.520 --> 06:44.550
No way!

06:45.120 --> 06:48.240
We're out of potatoes? But I know we had some!

06:48.240 --> 06:50.720
You know I made croquettes two days ago!

06:50.720 --> 06:54.000
Oh, that's right! What now?

06:54.000 --> 06:56.000
There's plenty of sweet potatoes.

06:56.000 --> 06:57.720
Those won't work!

06:58.110 --> 07:00.190
What are you trying to make?

07:01.220 --> 07:02.650
Meat and potatoes.

07:03.080 --> 07:04.110
Eh?

07:04.110 --> 07:05.880
Meat and potatoes!

07:06.280 --> 07:07.000
Huh?

07:07.000 --> 07:08.070
Huh?

07:08.070 --> 07:12.030
Wah! I wanted to surprise you, Ryuto!

07:12.030 --> 07:15.490
Huh? You were gonna make
meat and potatoes for me?

07:15.490 --> 07:17.630
Granny Sayo, I'll go buy some.

07:17.630 --> 07:18.570
I-I'll go too!

07:18.570 --> 07:19.710
Huh?

07:20.210 --> 07:21.990
I'll go with you.

07:22.670 --> 07:23.500
<b>Ishi</b>

07:22.670 --> 07:23.500
<b>da-ya</b>

07:22.670 --> 07:23.500
<b>Automatic</b>

07:27.590 --> 07:29.800
<b>Fruits & Vegetables</b>

07:27.590 --> 07:29.800
<b>Goya</b>

07:27.590 --> 07:29.800
<b>Whole
Watermelon</b>

07:27.590 --> 07:29.800
<b>Tonight's Side Dishes</b>

07:29.800 --> 07:31.140
There they are!

07:29.800 --> 07:31.880
<b>Potatoes</b>

07:34.920 --> 07:36.790
Let me carry that.

07:37.240 --> 07:38.850
It's light. I'm okay.

07:38.850 --> 07:41.810
Yeah, but then we can't hold hands.

07:46.190 --> 07:47.930
That's more like it.

07:55.170 --> 07:56.910
I want to help.

07:56.910 --> 07:58.440
Oh, that's oka—

07:58.900 --> 08:01.620
Uh, maybe the carrots, then.

08:01.620 --> 08:03.180
S-Sure.

08:03.180 --> 08:04.590
Chopped, not diced.

08:04.590 --> 08:06.590
Chopped... not diced?

08:10.260 --> 08:14.010
We carried the groceries together 
and now we're cooking together.

08:14.710 --> 08:17.800
It's almost like we're a married couple.

08:17.800 --> 08:20.510
Marr... marr... arr?!

08:21.020 --> 08:22.980
It's done!

08:22.980 --> 08:24.940
Wanna taste it?

08:24.940 --> 08:25.770
Huh?

08:27.590 --> 08:28.920
Say aah!

08:30.580 --> 08:32.710
Aah.

08:35.560 --> 08:37.120
It's great!

08:37.700 --> 08:39.580
Oh, good!

08:40.060 --> 08:44.020
I really didn't get it until now,

08:44.580 --> 08:49.040
but dating someone can 
actually be really wonderful.

08:49.990 --> 08:50.920
Yeah.

08:57.830 --> 08:59.180
I'm back.

08:59.180 --> 09:03.140
Welcome home, Maria. Was the library empty?

09:03.140 --> 09:05.050
It was pretty crowded.

09:05.050 --> 09:06.100
Really?

09:06.380 --> 09:09.310
Oh, I got a call from Granny Sayo.

09:09.310 --> 09:12.190
She asked when we're going to visit this year.

09:12.190 --> 09:16.290
Should we time it for the summer 
festival like always?

09:16.290 --> 09:17.490
Mm-hmm.

09:17.490 --> 09:21.700
She said that Runa's there this year, 
so they're keeping busy.

09:23.400 --> 09:24.560
Oh.

09:24.560 --> 09:28.510
And something about a boy from 
Runa's class being there with her.

09:28.920 --> 09:33.600
What was his name again? 
Ryo-kun or Ryu-kun or something.

09:33.600 --> 09:36.780
I'm sorry, Mom! I totally forgot.

09:36.780 --> 09:40.510
I promised to meet a friend 
from my old school that week.

09:40.510 --> 09:41.370
Huh?

09:41.370 --> 09:43.960
I don't think I can make it this year.

09:43.960 --> 09:46.330
Will you tell Granny Sayo that I'm sorry?

09:54.480 --> 09:57.700
Huh? Maria and Mom can't come?

09:57.700 --> 10:01.660
Sounds like she had other plans. 
It's really too bad.

10:01.660 --> 10:06.310
With Ryu-kun here this year, I thought 
the house would get nice and lively.

10:08.930 --> 10:12.460
I wonder if Maria is trying to avoid us.

10:12.460 --> 10:13.290
Yeah.

10:13.800 --> 10:19.980
I couldn't come last year, so I hadn't 
seen Maria for almost two years.

10:20.500 --> 10:22.700
We didn't stay in touch.

10:23.840 --> 10:25.930
So, when she transferred,

10:26.560 --> 10:28.520
I'm Kurose Maria.

10:28.520 --> 10:30.480
Whoa!

10:28.520 --> 10:30.480
<b><b>Kurose
Maria</b></b>

10:32.080 --> 10:35.980
it had been such a long time, 
I didn't even recognize her for a second.

10:36.570 --> 10:43.280
I had heard that Mom got a divorce and Maria 
stopped going to her private girls' school,

10:43.280 --> 10:46.120
but I had no idea 
she'd be coming to our school.

10:46.600 --> 10:48.220
Oh, really?

10:48.750 --> 10:55.360
For Maria, I bet she hates being in 
the same school, in the same class, as me.

10:55.360 --> 10:58.540
I thought she wouldn't want me to talk to her,

10:59.240 --> 11:03.670
so I didn't tell anyone but Nicole 
that she's my little sister.

11:08.070 --> 11:12.730
Maria and I have always had 
really different personalities,

11:16.980 --> 11:21.060
but I still like her a lot.

11:24.470 --> 11:29.930
I want to get along with her. 
Do you think that would be difficult?

11:31.010 --> 11:36.330
I think Kurose-san still needs a little time,

11:38.400 --> 11:42.840
but I think she can understand 
where you're coming from.

11:44.050 --> 11:45.000
Yeah.

11:47.810 --> 11:49.020
Hey, Ryuto.

11:50.280 --> 11:54.980
It might sound really weird 
to hear me saying this,

11:54.980 --> 12:00.690
but if we can, will you become 
Maria's friend with me?

12:01.280 --> 12:02.680
What do you mean?

12:02.680 --> 12:05.920
If I'm too direct, she'll probably reject me.

12:05.920 --> 12:10.040
So I won't be her sister. 
I'll try to start out by being her friend.

12:10.040 --> 12:17.400
Um, so you want to become friends without 
anyone finding out that you're sisters?

12:17.400 --> 12:18.500
Is that it?

12:18.500 --> 12:21.470
Yeah! I'll call it "The Friendship Project"!

12:21.470 --> 12:25.320
I'll get closer bit by bit, and then 
maybe when winter rolls around,

12:25.320 --> 12:28.180
I'll be able to hang out 
with Maria normally again.

12:28.180 --> 12:31.140
I want to share ice cream
 with her like before!

12:31.140 --> 12:36.610
Wow, suddenly I'm excited for 
the new term! I'm gonna do it!

12:39.700 --> 12:41.040
I'm back.

12:41.040 --> 12:42.530
Oh, Mao-kun!

12:43.510 --> 12:45.990
Welcome home. We saved you some dinner.

12:45.990 --> 12:48.160
Your phone is back from the shop.

12:50.040 --> 12:51.830
<b>Heeey! You alive~               ?</b>

12:50.040 --> 12:52.550
It's been way too long!

12:53.460 --> 12:54.710
<b>Akari</b>

12:54.770 --> 12:55.900
<b>Um um um.................... umm</b>

12:54.770 --> 12:55.900
<b>...you good?</b>

12:54.770 --> 12:57.750
<b><b>Akari</b></b>

12:58.250 --> 13:01.210
I've got a billion unread messages.

13:03.250 --> 13:07.100
How am I gonna catch up to all the trends?

13:08.340 --> 13:11.180
<i>I couldn't keep up with them to begin with.</i>

13:19.200 --> 13:21.050
Oh my god, this is sick!

13:23.600 --> 13:25.100
Hey, let's do it too, Ryuto!

13:25.100 --> 13:25.880
Huh?!

13:27.240 --> 13:37.000
Love You Tender!

13:44.460 --> 13:46.680
Great job these two weeks.

13:44.460 --> 13:46.680
<b>{blur1}Onjuku Summer
 Festival</b>

13:44.460 --> 13:46.680
<b>Fireworks
Display</b>

13:48.390 --> 13:50.140
Huh? What's this for?

13:50.140 --> 13:51.600
Your pay.

13:51.600 --> 13:55.310
Huh?! You let me stay for free. I can't.

13:55.310 --> 14:00.300
With you helping out, I was 
able to get a ton of other stuff done.

14:00.300 --> 14:03.780
See this? I know I don't look like it, 
but I'm actually a writer.

14:03.780 --> 14:05.660
Oh.

14:05.660 --> 14:07.010
Thanks, okay?

14:07.010 --> 14:09.000
Th-Thank you very much.

14:10.690 --> 14:14.450
<i>It's the first time
I've earned money by myself!</i>

14:14.450 --> 14:17.410
So, isn't today your two-month anniversary?

14:17.410 --> 14:19.200
H-How did you know that?

14:19.200 --> 14:24.700
Use those funds to give her 
a big surprise at tonight's festival!

14:25.590 --> 14:30.050
<b>Frankfurts</b>

14:25.590 --> 14:30.050
<b>Goldfish
Scooping</b>

14:25.590 --> 14:30.050
<b>Cheese Corn Dog</b>

14:30.050 --> 14:33.020
But what kind of surprise?

14:33.020 --> 14:37.580
Do they have anything that would 
make Shirakawa-san happy?

14:44.760 --> 14:45.620
Oh.

14:47.780 --> 14:49.600
<i>Ryuto, where are you?</i>

14:49.600 --> 14:51.160
I just got home.

14:51.160 --> 14:52.810
<i>Don't open the door yet!</i>

14:52.810 --> 14:53.620
Huh?

14:55.720 --> 14:57.390
<i>Okay, go ahead.</i>

14:57.390 --> 14:59.330
Okay...

15:07.800 --> 15:12.800
I just had Granny Sayo dress me.
 How do I look?

15:13.520 --> 15:16.510
You... look cute.

15:16.510 --> 15:20.430
A-ha! You had a lot bigger reaction 
to the swimsuit! Ryuto, you perv!

15:20.430 --> 15:24.110
Huh? No, I didn't!
 I think you look super cute!

15:24.110 --> 15:25.860
I wonder about that.

15:25.860 --> 15:27.480
It's the truth!

15:27.480 --> 15:31.100
We have a yukata for you too, 
so get changed and let's go to the festival!

15:31.100 --> 15:32.660
Huh? You do?

15:42.320 --> 15:43.960
Wait up!

15:46.290 --> 15:48.940
Ho! I got another one!

15:48.940 --> 15:50.920
Okay, here I go.

15:53.720 --> 15:55.150
You can do it, Ryuto!

15:55.150 --> 15:56.640
Yeah.

15:59.140 --> 16:00.860
I remember this!

16:01.700 --> 16:02.640
Huh?

16:12.740 --> 16:15.260
Shirakawa-san, aren't your feet tired?

16:15.260 --> 16:16.950
No, I'm fine.

16:18.640 --> 16:21.470
Oh. Can you hold our place in line a minute?

16:21.470 --> 16:22.150
Sure.

16:25.800 --> 16:27.880
Cute!

16:30.480 --> 16:32.960
Do you have a ring with moonstone?

16:32.960 --> 16:36.010
Oh, I'm sorry! We're all sold out.

16:36.010 --> 16:37.920
Aww, too bad.

16:37.920 --> 16:40.220
We'll probably be back next year.

16:40.220 --> 16:42.420
Okay. I'll come again.

16:48.950 --> 16:50.400
Are your feet okay?

16:50.400 --> 16:54.470
Yeah. But Ryuto, you keep asking that.

16:54.470 --> 16:58.990
Sorry. I've never walked 
with a girl in a yukata before.

16:58.990 --> 17:00.380
Thanks, I'm honored!

17:02.440 --> 17:05.370
Oh, right. I guess it is your first time.

17:05.750 --> 17:09.740
Yeah. I haven't been to a festival 
since elementary school.

17:09.740 --> 17:12.180
I'd never even eaten a cheese corn dog before.

17:13.080 --> 17:14.360
Huh.

17:16.680 --> 17:20.680
I always thought candied apples 
looked hard to eat,

17:20.680 --> 17:22.920
but now that I've tried one, 
I know they're delicious.

17:25.270 --> 17:30.230
Now that I think of it, our date was 
also my first time trying bubble tea.

17:31.000 --> 17:32.710
Oh yeah?

17:35.250 --> 17:41.140
The first thing my dad ever bought 
for my mom was a candied apple.

17:41.620 --> 17:42.950
Oh, was it?

17:43.840 --> 17:49.830
I told you before, but I always dreamed that 
I would marry the first person I dated,

17:49.830 --> 17:51.600
just like my mom did.

17:51.600 --> 17:52.440
Yeah.

17:59.090 --> 18:00.470
Shirakawa-san?

18:02.430 --> 18:03.750
Shirakawa-san?

18:05.360 --> 18:08.970
Why can't this be my first time?

18:10.040 --> 18:16.140
I see how new this all is for you, 
and for some reason, it makes me so sad.

18:16.140 --> 18:16.940
Huh?

18:18.870 --> 18:21.910
It isn't the first time for me.

18:22.520 --> 18:29.500
Walking with a boy in yukata, 
eating cheese corn dogs, scooping goldfish...

18:30.130 --> 18:33.090
I wish it was my first time!

18:35.050 --> 18:38.310
I wish it was all the first time 
for both of us!

18:39.760 --> 18:42.760
I want to erase my memory!

18:43.560 --> 18:49.660
You've had so many first experiences with me, 
and that makes me so happy,

18:49.660 --> 18:53.700
but I don't have any first times 
to share with you.

18:55.940 --> 18:57.290
But you do.

18:59.700 --> 19:02.070
You've shared a lot with me.

19:02.660 --> 19:05.340
Even if you've experienced 
something with someone else,

19:06.000 --> 19:10.700
if you feel something new 
and different when you do it with me,

19:11.610 --> 19:14.380
then I'm happy. Really happy.

19:17.320 --> 19:23.450
When we had our bubble tea date, when we 
rode the boats, when we went to the beach...

19:24.280 --> 19:29.100
Every single time, you shared 
those feelings with me.

19:30.640 --> 19:32.000
Ryuto...

19:34.180 --> 19:37.220
Here. For our two-month anniversary.

19:37.960 --> 19:39.930
You remembered?

19:42.600 --> 19:45.450
What... a moonstone?

19:45.450 --> 19:48.620
I saw it on my way back to the house earlier.

19:48.620 --> 19:51.920
I picked it because it reminded me of you.

19:52.550 --> 19:55.020
I didn't know your birthstone or anything...

19:57.840 --> 20:03.530
I know it isn't enough compared to everything 
you've shared with me, but still—

20:03.530 --> 20:04.980
It is enough!

20:05.550 --> 20:08.840
It's more than enough. Thank you.

20:09.350 --> 20:14.070
Meeting you was the best 
present I've ever gotten, Ryuto.

20:16.980 --> 20:19.000
It's so pretty!

20:19.000 --> 20:23.700
Shirakawa-san, from now on 
let's try a lot of new things together.

20:23.700 --> 20:28.140
We lived in totally different 
worlds until we started dating,

20:28.140 --> 20:31.080
so if we feel like it, 
there's still lots for us to do.

20:31.080 --> 20:33.160
New experiences to have together.

20:33.160 --> 20:35.160
Yeah, you're right!

20:35.160 --> 20:38.260
Let's do a ton of new things together!

20:40.610 --> 20:42.660
This really is pretty.

20:50.010 --> 20:52.780
Wow! We got VIP seats!

20:52.780 --> 20:53.980
We did!

21:01.880 --> 21:04.840
Can I stay like this until the fireworks end?

21:04.840 --> 21:06.360
Uh, yeah.

21:08.580 --> 21:10.360
When people's feelings get closer,

21:10.360 --> 21:13.530
it's natural for them to want 
to be closer to each other.

21:13.530 --> 21:16.060
I realized that after we started dating.

21:17.100 --> 21:22.060
I like you, Ryuto. If this feeling 
continues growing, I'm sure that

21:22.470 --> 21:25.450
